Note on duplicate key detection: PyYAML's SafeLoader silently overrides duplicates. I'll implement:

```python
class DupKeySafeLoader(yaml.SafeLoader): pass
def _construct_mapping(loader, node, deep=False):
    keys = set()
    for k, v in node.value:
        kk = loader.construct_object(k, deep=deep)
        if kk in keys:
            raise yaml.constructor.ConstructorError(None,None,f"duplicate key: {kk}", k.start_mark)
        keys.add(kk)
    return yaml.SafeLoader.construct_mapping(loader, node, deep=deep)
DupKeySafeLoader.add_constructor(yaml.resolver.BaseResolver.DEFAULT_MAPPING_TAG, _construct_mapping)
```

Careful: construct_object on key then construct_mapping again reconstructs; fine for our purposes (small file). Actually calling construct_object twice can cause issues with anchors; simpler: iterate node.value, construct key, check duplicates, then call super().construct_mapping. Standard recipe. OK.

